Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day: a month flipped. By
4 October the desk had **412 reports**.

**Merged as one issue, but it holds three.** The parser reads dates month first, and our
tenants write the day first: that fix is queued. Two more problems came in under the same
subjects: booking-v3's date hint, and a one-day shift across time zones. Each has its own ticket
now; see [three problems, not one](/kb/incidents/4471/problems).

<Callout kind="warn">
Split, and closed by engineering on 5 October: parser fixed, hint won't fix (booking-v3 form
retired). The one-day shift has no fix yet; its ticket stays open.
</Callout>

